## General entries akana adds to Zemberek's dictionaries (previously built into dictionary.rs).
istemci
Akana [P:Noun,Prop]

## Letter names (Zemberek's plain nouns for F, G, J, P and Ş) take no suffix written out: a
## letter's suffixes follow the letter and an apostrophe (G'ye), as its abbreviation entry reads.
## Without this geler, peler and the like read as plurals of the letter.
fe [A:NoSuffix]
ge [A:NoSuffix]
je [A:NoSuffix]
pe [A:NoSuffix]
şe [A:NoSuffix]

## Verbs that also read as a voice derivation of another verb (katıl-dı / kat-ıl-dı, alın-an /
## al-ın-an). Both readings are in every word that has one, so corpus counts cannot rank them;
## these entries do. Lexicalized: the verb's own meaning is the usual one (katılmak "join", not
## kat-ıl "be added"; kaynaklanmak "arise from", not kaynakla-n "be welded"). NotLexicalized:
## its forms are mostly the plain derivation (alınan "taken", sürülen "put forward", dinlen-
## "be heard" in court text). Chosen from the contexts in the court sample; verbs whose uses
## are mixed (ayrılmak, çekilmek, taşınmak, yenmek, yayılmak, dinlenmek) are left to the prior.
anlatmak [A:Lexicalized]
aksatmak [A:Lexicalized]
arttırmak [A:Lexicalized]
ayaklanmak [A:Lexicalized]
azaltmak [A:Lexicalized]
bastırmak [A:Lexicalized]
belirtmek [A:Lexicalized]
bildirmek [A:Lexicalized]
bindirmek [A:Lexicalized]
boşanmak [A:Lexicalized]
bulundurmak [A:Lexicalized]
bulunmak [A:Lexicalized]
büyütmek [A:Lexicalized]
caydırmak [A:Lexicalized]
çıkartmak [A:Lexicalized]
