## Rare verbs whose forms coincide with a frequent word's (bula-ma-dığı / bul-ama-dığı "that he
## could not find", il-iş / iliş, ay-an / ayan): any other reading of the word outranks them.
aymak [A:Rare]
bulamak [A:Rare]
ilmek [A:Rare]

## Compounds whose Roots: Zemberek misspells or truncates (review 2, MLEX2-08); the build now
## checks that a compound's parts spell it. Words it marks CompoundP3sg that have no possessive
## of their own (acemlale, üstderi) are plain nouns, and ortaparmak "middle finger" is no verb.
tavuskuyruğu [A:CompoundP3sg; Roots:tavus-kuyruk]
bacabaşı [A:CompoundP3sg; Roots:baca-baş]
güveyfeneri [A:CompoundP3sg; Roots:güvey-fener]
hasekiküpesi [A:CompoundP3sg; Roots:haseki-küpe]
havvaanaeli [A:CompoundP3sg; Roots:havvaana-el]
borazancıbaşı [A:CompoundP3sg; Roots:borazancı-baş]
aşçıbaşı [A:CompoundP3sg; Roots:aşçı-baş]
düşkırıklığı [A:CompoundP3sg; Roots:düş-kırıklık]
elbirliği [A:CompoundP3sg; Roots:el-birlik]
elyazması [A:CompoundP3sg; Roots:el-yazma]
elyazması [P:Adj; A:CompoundP3sg; Roots:el-yazma]
güvenoylaması [A:CompoundP3sg; Roots:güven-oylama]
sözvarlığı [A:CompoundP3sg; Roots:söz-varlık]
yabanasması [A:CompoundP3sg; Roots:yaban-asma]
acemlale
acıçiğdem
acıyonca
üstderi
ortaparmak [P:Noun]

## General vocabulary the dictionaries lack (plan step E6, review 2 MLEX2-07): -sI adjectives,
## and words of the last years with the pronunciation their suffixes follow.
çocuksu [P:Adj]
kadınsı [P:Adj]
erkeksi [P:Adj]
insansı [P:Adj]
koronavirüs
kovid
COVID [P:Abbrv; Pr:kovid; Ref:kovid]
PCR [P:Abbrv]
NFT [P:Abbrv]
SİHA [P:Abbrv; Pr:siha]
blokzincir
gigabayt
dron
fintek
özçekim
karekod
emoji
otogaz
## Common spellings of words the dictionary writes otherwise (takoğraf 15 sample tokens against
## takograf 3); the lemma stays the dictionary's.
takoğraf [Ref:takograf]
asteroid [Ref:asteroit]

## Clothing sizes, which are no Roman numerals (XL'i as iksel beside Zemberek's ikslarç); TL
## read as lira as well as tele (TL'nın 53 sample tokens, TL'nin 3,831). Plan step D4.
XS [P:Abbrv]
XL [P:Abbrv; Pr:iksel; Index:1]
XXL [P:Abbrv]
TL [P:Abbrv; Pr:lira; Index:1]

## Abbreviations written in lower case (bkz 4,100 training tokens against 140 capitalised, md
## 2,269, vb 651, vs 371, cm 277, kg 217, km 185, mm 87): their dictionary spelling, which a word
## written in lower case is checked against (plan step D7; the readings of bü, si or la, junk
## abbreviations in capitals, do not count for one). md and mad read as madde.
bkz [P:Abbrv; Pr:bekeze]
md [P:Abbrv; Pr:madde]
mad [P:Abbrv; Pr:madde]
vb [P:Abbrv; Pr:vebe]
vs [P:Abbrv; Pr:vese]
sy [P:Abbrv; Pr:seye]
par [P:Abbrv]
cm [P:Abbrv; Pr:ceme]
mm [P:Abbrv; Pr:meme]
km [P:Abbrv; Pr:keme]
kg [P:Abbrv; Pr:kege]
mg [P:Abbrv; Pr:mege]
ml [P:Abbrv; Pr:mele]
lt [P:Abbrv; Pr:lete]
sn [P:Abbrv; Pr:sene]
kr [P:Abbrv; Pr:kere]

## Lexicalised derivations (plan step C6, review 2 RANK2-04). A derivation that spells a word the
## dictionary lists yields to it (the analyzer's lexicalised_derivations), so that the word's lemma
## no longer turns with every re-estimation of the prior: başvurucu was başvur-ucu or başvuru-cu
## (0.36 / 0.30 / 0.30), uyuşmazlık uyuş-mazlık or uyuş-maz-lık, yüklenici yüklen-ici twice.
başvurucu [P:Noun]
uyuşmazlık [P:Noun]
yüklenici [P:Noun]
## Verbal nouns in -mA the dictionary lists as nouns: Lexicalized where the noun is the word meant
## (görüşme "meeting", açıklama "statement", çarpma "collision"; açıklaması read 0.47 / 0.47),
## Rare where it is another word (dolma "stuffed dish": sürenin dolması is dol-ma).
görüşme [P:Noun; A:Lexicalized]
açıklama [P:Noun; A:Lexicalized]
çarpma [P:Noun; A:Lexicalized]
dolma [P:Noun; A:Rare]
## Causatives of -lAn and -lAş verbs that are words of their own (görevlendirmek "assign", not
## görevlen-dir "make take up a post"), which Zemberek lacks.
görevlendirmek [A:Lexicalized]
birleştirmek [A:Lexicalized]
bilgilendirmek [A:Lexicalized]

## dolayı as a noun, for its possessive forms (dolayısı ile, dolayısıyla): Zemberek has only the
## postposition (plan step F, review 2 MORPH2-16).
dolayı [P:Noun]
